  "details": "Chatbox position is nameplate-based now, and the setting labels were updated for it:\n\n144732 - \"Set chatbox to above nameplate position\"\n\n144736 - \"Set chatbox to below nameplate position\"\n\nBut the alerts that show up when you change the setting still use the old wording:\n\n24625 - \"Chatbox display position set to above head\"\n\n144730 - \"Chatbox display position set to below\"\n\n24625 says \"head\" while the setting says \"nameplate\", so the alert doesn't match the option you just picked.\n\n144730 is the bigger problem - below what? As a Korean translator I can't leave it as a bare \"below\", I have to write either below the head or below the nameplate, and there's no way to tell which one it means.",
